# Riziki Industrial Chemicals — the whole public face on one server.
#
# DO NOT MOVE, RENAME OR DELETE THIS FILE. The shared proxy mounts it.
#
# This server carries sixteen sites behind one proxy, `edge-caddy` in
# /srv/edge, which owns ports 80 and 443. Its config begins:
#
#     # The POS project's own Caddyfile is imported read-only straight from
#     # its repo, so that team keeps control of their sites and nothing here
#     # needs editing when they change them. Everything else lives in ./sites.
#     import /etc/caddy/riziki.caddy
#     import /etc/caddy/sites/*.caddy
#
# `/etc/caddy/riziki.caddy` IS THIS FILE, bind-mounted read-only out of the
# repo. So these blocks are live on the shared edge the moment the edge
# reloads — this is not a copy of anything and nothing has to be installed.
#
# It was moved once, to deploy/edge/rizikichemicals.caddy, on the belief that
# every app contributed a file to /srv/edge/sites/. That import line had not
# been read. The mount went dangling, Riziki's three hostnames left the edge's
# config, the shop system answered 502 and the bare domain fell through to
# another site on the box. Three certificates and a live till turned on one
# `git mv`. Put nothing in /srv/edge/sites/ for this project — it is imported
# from here, and two files claiming one hostname is a config the edge refuses
# to load AT ALL, which takes every other site with it.
#
# Three sites, three certificates, all fetched and renewed by the edge on its
# own. The only prerequisite is DNS: A records for rizikichemicals.co.ke,
# www.rizikichemicals.co.ke and pos.rizikichemicals.co.ke, all pointing at
# this server's IP.
#
# THE UPSTREAMS ARE CONTAINER NAMES, NOT SERVICE NAMES, AND THAT IS THE BUG
# THIS FILE WAS CARRYING.
#
# The marketing site used to point at `web:80`. `web` is a compose service
# name, and the edge is attached to several projects' networks at once — so
# from inside the edge, `web` is whatever Docker's DNS feels like returning
# among every container on those networks answering to that alias. At least
# one other project on this box runs a website service called `web`, and the
# shop's own domain spent weeks serving that other client's site. The till
# never broke, because `pos` happens to be a name nobody else uses.
#
# A container name is unique across the whole daemon. `riziki-pos-web-1` can
# only ever be this project's website. If the compose project directory is
# ever renamed the container name moves with it, so check it after any such
# rename:
#   docker compose ps --format '{{.Name}}'

# The marketing site. The pages themselves live in the `web` container, built
# from apps/riziki-web on every deploy; this block only terminates HTTPS for it.
rizikichemicals.co.ke {
	reverse_proxy riziki-pos-web-1:80
}

# One canonical host: www redirects rather than serving a duplicate site.
www.rizikichemicals.co.ke {
	redir https://rizikichemicals.co.ke{uri} permanent
}

# The shop system.
pos.rizikichemicals.co.ke {
	# Left as the service name because it is what is live and working, and a
	# name no other project here uses. Worth making `riziki-pos-pos-1` the next
	# time this file is touched with the shop closed.
	reverse_proxy pos:3100
	encode zstd gzip
}
